# FathomDB shellcheck configuration — 0.8.21 Slice 30 (SHELLCHECK), per
# dev/design/ci-verify-robustness-review.md R1.1.
#
# This file records the repo's DELIBERATE ENABLES only. It intentionally
# contains no `disable=` line: a repo-level `disable=` is indistinguishable
# from "covered" while covering nothing, which is the exact posture that let
# the same SIGPIPE/masked-return bug through four times. Where a finding is
# genuinely wrong for a specific site, the suppression is a narrowly scoped
# `# shellcheck disable=SCxxxx` on that line with a reason.
#
# Enforcement lives in scripts/agent-lint-shell.sh (invoked by
# scripts/agent-lint.sh); the pin lives in scripts/lib/shellcheck-version.sh.
# Editors that read .shellcheckrc therefore see the same enabled check set the
# gate does.

# SC2312. OPTIONAL in shellcheck (off unless requested) and the single check
# that catches this repo's historical failure mode: a command whose non-zero
# exit is swallowed because it is inside a command substitution or upstream of
# a pipe (`cmd | head` under `set -o pipefail` -> SIGPIPE -> the gate passes on
# a crashed producer). Slice 25 was the FOURTH hand-fix of that class.
#
# Coverage is ratcheted, not blanket: scripts/agent-lint-shell.sh enforces
# SC2312 over every tracked *.sh EXCEPT the files listed in
# scripts/shellcheck-sc2312-ratchet.txt, and that list can only shrink (a file
# that has become clean must be removed or the gate fails). New files are
# covered by default.
enable=check-extra-masked-returns

# Follow `. "$SCRIPT_DIR/lib/foo.sh"` into the sourced file instead of emitting
# SC1091 "not following". This makes the existing `# shellcheck source=` header
# directives (43 of them already in the tree) actually load-bearing, and lets
# shellcheck see variables/functions defined in scripts/lib/*.sh — strictly
# MORE analysis, not less.
external-sources=true
source-path=SCRIPTDIR
